==English==
{{wikipedia|Split}}

===Etymology===
Attested since about 1567, from {{bor|en|dum|splitten||to split}} and/or {{bor|en|gml|splitten||to split}}, both ultimately from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*splittjan}}, an intensive form of {{der|en|gmw-pro|*splītan|t=to split}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*splītaną}} (whence {{cog|da|splitte}}, {{cog|nds|splieten}}, {{cog|de|spleißen}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)pley-||to split, splice}}.

Compare {{cog|ang|speld||splinter}}, {{cog|goh|spaltan||to split}}, {{cog|sga|sliss||splinter}}, {{cog|lt|spaliai||flax sheaves}}, {{cog|cs|půl||half}}, {{cog|cu|расплитати|рас-плитати|to cleave, split}}.

